WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.230
<i>Year 1951 of the northern calendar</i>

00:05.230 --> 00:07.530
Rossa.

00:14.940 --> 00:18.240
Are you going to... -

00:18.240 --> 00:20.640
- leave me behind?

00:22.640 --> 00:24.850
You keep falling behind.

00:24.850 --> 00:26.980
We won't make it in time.

00:26.980 --> 00:29.820
Wait up!

00:29.820 --> 00:33.020
Couldn't you have found an easier way?

00:33.020 --> 00:35.390
Your dad was a hunter, right?

00:38.060 --> 00:41.900
It's not like I'm familiar with <i>these</i> forests!

00:41.900 --> 00:44.000
Huh?

00:44.000 --> 00:45.900
Those sons of bitches at the garrison...

00:45.900 --> 00:49.710
Why did they have to give us that clunker?

00:49.710 --> 00:54.010
The wolves' cipher may have been a bit too much for me.

00:54.010 --> 00:58.380
No, Testa. You're a professor, aren't you?

00:58.380 --> 01:00.750
Surely you're able to decode the Luger Code.

01:00.750 --> 01:03.450
That's why I recommended you.

01:03.450 --> 01:07.320
Like I suspected, we have to capture a werewolf -

01:07.320 --> 01:10.820
- and talk to it to be able to understand the code.

01:14.630 --> 01:16.770
Just hurry up!

01:16.770 --> 01:20.870
We have to get to them before they dispose of it.

01:20.870 --> 01:24.570
Hey, wait up!

01:30.610 --> 01:33.320
Come on!

01:36.920 --> 01:38.990
Pick up the pace, damn it!

01:45.530 --> 01:51.430
The war between humans ended ten and some years ago.

01:53.070 --> 01:57.310
The next enemy was -

01:57.310 --> 02:00.010
- not human.

02:01.510 --> 02:07.510
Luger Code 1951

02:11.190 --> 02:15.020
It's your fault!

02:15.020 --> 02:17.790
Do you know how many people have died?

02:17.790 --> 02:20.830
You!

02:20.830 --> 02:23.600
Because of your kind!

02:27.800 --> 02:32.000
I'll say you tried to escape and I had to dispose of you.

02:35.240 --> 02:38.350
Revenge! Die in pain!

02:38.350 --> 02:41.520
Stop. Lower your weapon.

02:41.520 --> 02:45.820
Who are you?

02:45.820 --> 02:47.860
Hey, what's this?

02:47.860 --> 02:50.430
This is a precious sample.

02:50.430 --> 02:53.060
Are you OK?

02:53.060 --> 02:56.060
Who are you guys?

02:56.060 --> 02:58.800
You should have heard about it.

02:58.800 --> 03:00.840
We will take her.

03:02.600 --> 03:04.310
Sorry about that.

03:04.310 --> 03:07.340
I'm not kind enough to just shoot the gun off your hands.

03:07.340 --> 03:10.340
Shit!

03:12.910 --> 03:15.420
What we need now is -

03:15.420 --> 03:18.950
- real geniuses. If you are not one, -

03:18.950 --> 03:21.960
- go home and do crossword puzzles for all I care.

03:21.960 --> 03:24.360
Listen to me, Lt. Col. Curtis!

03:24.360 --> 03:27.830
I know he's a bit strange, -

03:27.830 --> 03:31.400
- but his linguistic and ethnological insights -

03:31.400 --> 03:33.500
- are nothing but genius!

03:33.500 --> 03:36.400
And from such a young age!

03:40.510 --> 03:45.650
When the snowfall stops, we'll head for the airfield in your truck.

03:45.650 --> 03:48.020
We'll hand you over to the military police.

03:48.020 --> 03:50.690
You'll probably be court martialed.

03:50.690 --> 03:53.490
Be aware of that.

03:59.360 --> 04:01.360
Cheap liquor.

04:01.360 --> 04:03.700
Could you not get anything better?

04:03.700 --> 04:05.800
You piece of shit.

04:05.800 --> 04:09.240
There's really nothing we can use, Rossa.

04:09.240 --> 04:12.870
There were some bandages, but besides that only tools.

04:12.870 --> 04:17.010
Some kind of cans, strange gadgets and random bullets.

04:17.010 --> 04:19.010
That's gunpowder.

04:19.010 --> 04:22.850
That device is for filling cartridges with gunpowder.

04:22.850 --> 04:24.350
Oh.

04:24.350 --> 04:27.790
This must be a hunter's shed.

04:27.790 --> 04:30.360
You would know, being a hunter's son after all!

04:30.790 --> 04:35.290
You... Would you mind not bringing it up all the time?

04:40.670 --> 04:43.270
So she's a werewolf.

04:46.170 --> 04:49.580
They're not often brought back alive.

04:49.580 --> 04:54.380
That's because they tend to take their own lives when caught.

04:54.380 --> 04:56.320
Excuse me...

04:56.320 --> 04:58.790
I heard that the Luger Code has been deciphered.

04:58.790 --> 05:01.790
Is it true?

05:01.790 --> 05:05.960
Who told you that?

05:05.960 --> 05:08.400
It's just a rumor that I heard.

05:08.400 --> 05:12.100
They're saying we can push the werewolves back now.

05:12.100 --> 05:13.600
Huh.

05:13.600 --> 05:16.500
We do have a theory.

05:18.410 --> 05:20.880
We just have to try it out in practice.

05:20.880 --> 05:23.710
That's why we need to talk to a werewolf.

05:23.710 --> 05:25.780
Try it out then, quickly!

05:25.780 --> 05:27.920
The key to the muzzle is in my pocket.

05:27.920 --> 05:31.550
Lance Corporal! Shut your mouth!

05:31.550 --> 05:34.390
Testa, do you want to try?

05:34.390 --> 05:39.560
We still have time before nightfall. She-wolves aren't known to transform anyway.

05:39.560 --> 05:41.060
You're right.

05:41.060 --> 05:44.760
I wanted to practice my listening before returning to the headquarters anyway.

06:13.160 --> 06:14.060
Hey!

06:33.620 --> 06:35.820
This little bitch...

06:41.460 --> 06:43.530
Huh?

06:43.530 --> 06:46.130
What was that?

06:46.130 --> 06:48.200
What is it?

06:48.200 --> 06:50.200
Ouch!

07:07.450 --> 07:09.520
A wolf?

07:14.920 --> 07:16.860
Damn it!

07:33.540 --> 07:35.840
Did you call upon your friends?

07:35.840 --> 07:37.740
Huh?

07:38.850 --> 07:41.220
I know nothing of your war.

07:42.220 --> 07:45.590
Just get eaten!

07:57.060 --> 07:58.370
It's no use!

07:58.370 --> 08:00.440
This shed will be torn to bits!

08:00.440 --> 08:04.040
We should have killed her when we had the chance!

08:04.040 --> 08:08.140
Cut her to pieces and show it to the wolves outside!

08:08.140 --> 08:10.250
You can't do that!

08:12.880 --> 08:15.550
Captain, please! We should not provoke them further.

08:15.550 --> 08:18.450
You coward. I'll kill her!

08:18.450 --> 08:21.020
Stop it!
- Out of my way!

08:35.240 --> 08:37.540
Don't kill her!

08:37.540 --> 08:41.680
We need her to figure out the Luger Code.

08:42.680 --> 08:46.150
Besides, we may be able to connect with her.

08:46.150 --> 08:50.350
I don't want to kill her.

08:50.350 --> 08:52.690
You fucking pussy.

08:52.690 --> 08:54.690
This is war!

08:54.690 --> 08:58.430
He's soft, I agree with you on that.

08:58.430 --> 09:01.430
But I cannot let you kill our prisoner.

09:01.430 --> 09:03.430
You pieces of shit!

09:06.600 --> 09:10.670
Captain!
- Shit!

09:10.670 --> 09:13.040
What are you doing?

09:13.040 --> 09:17.240
I'm not afraid of no monsters, so long as I have a gun!

09:18.650 --> 09:22.450
Stop!
- Give me that gun!

09:25.720 --> 09:27.720
Rossa!
- Let's go!

09:27.720 --> 09:31.090
Okay.

09:31.090 --> 09:33.030
I don't want to go!

09:33.030 --> 09:34.860
Captain, I can't.

09:34.860 --> 09:39.070
God damn chicken!
- Don't go out!

09:48.840 --> 09:50.950
Frank! Fucking monsters...

09:50.950 --> 09:53.480
Come at me!

09:55.480 --> 09:58.420
Testa! Get me the cans you saw!

09:58.420 --> 10:01.020
And a hammer!

10:05.730 --> 10:07.930
Rossa, what are you going to do?

10:10.600 --> 10:13.070
Let's go!

10:20.380 --> 10:23.310
There's no time! Leave her!

10:27.620 --> 10:30.290
Hey!

10:38.590 --> 10:41.090
Come.

10:42.860 --> 10:45.170
Let's go, quick!

11:30.180 --> 11:32.280
Rossa.

11:33.920 --> 11:36.080
What an explosion.

11:36.080 --> 11:39.950
That was an improvised time bomb.
- Time bomb?

11:39.950 --> 11:43.550
I used the heat to spark the percussion cap.

11:51.900 --> 11:56.070
Lance Corporal Balke. Your truck is nearby, isn't it?

11:56.070 --> 11:59.440
Yes. It's where we entered the forest.

11:59.440 --> 12:01.680
You can have this.

12:01.680 --> 12:05.450
Ow.
- That's what you get for being reckless.

12:05.450 --> 12:07.820
Well, you always have my back -

12:07.820 --> 12:10.750
- when push comes to shove.

12:10.750 --> 12:12.250
Get a grip.

12:12.250 --> 12:15.950
You'd better start taking care of yourself.

12:20.030 --> 12:23.030
Hurry. The sun will set soon.

12:23.030 --> 12:26.830
The werewolves transform after nightfall.

12:26.830 --> 12:30.330
We have to get to the airfield.

12:35.880 --> 12:37.880
Sorry.

12:40.350 --> 12:42.450
Yonaga.
- Huh?

12:42.450 --> 12:44.990
My name.

12:44.990 --> 12:47.790
I don't care about the war.

12:47.790 --> 12:50.590
I hate humans and werewolves equally.

12:50.590 --> 12:53.390
You wanna keep killing each other, go ahead.

12:53.390 --> 12:55.900
I won't cooperate.

12:55.900 --> 13:00.440
If you help us with the cipher, the situation will change.

13:00.440 --> 13:03.500
We might even be able to negotiate.

13:03.500 --> 13:05.640
That's what you want, right?

13:05.640 --> 13:08.410
A quick end to the war.

13:08.410 --> 13:11.510
That won't be enough for you humans.

13:11.510 --> 13:13.510
Yes it will.
- There!

13:13.510 --> 13:16.350
That's our truck!

13:16.350 --> 13:20.090
Humans cannot tolerate those better than them.

13:20.090 --> 13:22.690
They won't stop until werewolves are extinct.

13:24.730 --> 13:29.800
That's true. Humans can be cold to those different or better than them.

13:29.800 --> 13:34.470
There is discrimination and prejudice even between humans.

13:34.470 --> 13:38.140
I was bullied in boarding school, too.

13:38.140 --> 13:42.110
Just because I was a little better than the other students.

13:42.110 --> 13:46.350
To tell you the truth, I don't really care for the war either.

13:46.350 --> 13:48.520
The only reason I took on this job -

13:48.520 --> 13:51.520
- is so that I could repay Rossa's kindness.

13:57.990 --> 14:01.200
Too bad I can't decipher the Luger Code.

14:01.200 --> 14:03.200
Huh?

14:04.330 --> 14:08.500
Didn't you say you had a theory?
- Yes.

14:08.500 --> 14:11.540
My theory was that I can't decipher the code.

14:11.540 --> 14:14.710
Now it's more than a theory.

14:14.710 --> 14:17.750
Humans cannot decipher it.

14:17.750 --> 14:20.980
Luger Code is not only based on words.

14:20.980 --> 14:22.820
What does that mean?

14:22.820 --> 14:26.820
We also use our feelings. You need ears like mine to hear it.

14:29.760 --> 14:34.300
It's like telepathy, or like the mind.

14:34.300 --> 14:37.700
You send it out together with the sound.

14:37.700 --> 14:40.330
That's why only we can decipher it.

14:40.330 --> 14:42.840
But I won't help you.

14:42.840 --> 14:44.840
That's how it is.

14:44.840 --> 14:48.510
I'm sorry I couldn't be of help, Rossa.

14:48.510 --> 14:50.510
I see.

14:50.510 --> 14:53.810
That's good enough for me.

14:55.580 --> 14:58.490
Lance Corporal Balke. What is this?

14:58.490 --> 15:01.760
Balke? I -

15:01.760 --> 15:04.760
- devoured him the other day!

15:05.790 --> 15:07.630
Balke?
- Get back!

15:56.110 --> 16:00.250
Thank you.

16:00.250 --> 16:01.950
It's not over yet!

16:43.690 --> 16:45.790
Get in!

16:45.790 --> 16:50.230
What was that? Why did he try to kill you too?

16:50.230 --> 16:52.230
Aren't you one of their kind?

16:52.230 --> 16:55.200
Why was Balke - no - the werewolf -

16:55.200 --> 16:57.510
- in there with the others?

16:59.140 --> 17:03.040
They made me into a bait.
- A bait?

17:03.040 --> 17:06.910
They had heard that humans had deciphered the Luger Code.

17:06.910 --> 17:09.780
They wanted to see if it was true and made me into a bait.

17:09.780 --> 17:11.920
To get you to come.

17:11.920 --> 17:13.920
Since he figured you hadn't actually deciphered it, -

17:13.920 --> 17:16.790
- he must have wanted to get rid of me too.

17:16.790 --> 17:19.890
Why would they use one of their kind as a bait?

17:19.890 --> 17:24.530
That's because my blood is cursed.

17:24.530 --> 17:27.570
Cursed?
- Blood?

17:43.880 --> 17:47.180
T.. Testa...

18:19.120 --> 18:22.620
Monster or not, the eyes get you.

18:27.830 --> 18:30.260
Oh shit!

18:32.470 --> 18:34.800
I have to get as far as possible...

18:34.800 --> 18:37.500
Rossa...

18:56.320 --> 18:58.390
Rossa.

18:58.390 --> 19:00.930
I.. It's because -

19:00.930 --> 19:03.930
- I said I could decipher it...

19:07.030 --> 19:09.500
Do you want to save him?
- Huh?

19:09.500 --> 19:12.870
Answer me. Tell me straight.

19:12.870 --> 19:14.880
I want to save him.

19:14.880 --> 19:18.550
I want to save Rossa!

19:18.550 --> 19:21.650
Then die.

19:31.160 --> 19:36.300
You will become one that is hunted by both men and werewolves.

19:36.300 --> 19:39.900
This cursed blood will flow through your veins.

19:42.140 --> 19:45.510
The hateful energy will make your heart beat again!

19:55.620 --> 19:58.620
So this is the end.

20:00.050 --> 20:03.960
I hope they got away.

20:23.080 --> 20:25.080
T... Testa?

21:37.690 --> 21:41.090
My prayer is... -

21:43.260 --> 21:45.260
- from this day on, a curse!

22:08.780 --> 22:13.290
So you won't come back to the civilization?

22:13.290 --> 22:16.420
I'm sorry. I can't, like this.

22:16.420 --> 22:18.730
I'd just cause trouble for the people around me.

22:18.730 --> 22:21.430
The werewolves will be back soon, in greater numbers.

22:21.430 --> 22:23.760
Not only them.

22:23.760 --> 22:26.200
Humans will hunt us as well.

22:30.470 --> 22:34.070
This is it, Rossa. Be well.

22:37.080 --> 22:39.080
Wait.

22:39.080 --> 22:42.180
You shouldn't get up!

22:42.180 --> 22:44.220
Help will come for you soon.

22:44.220 --> 22:46.750
Rossa...

22:46.750 --> 22:49.060
At least hide your ears.

22:49.060 --> 22:53.260
I'm just lending it to you. You'll bring it back one day.

22:53.260 --> 22:56.460
Okay?
- Rossa...

22:56.460 --> 22:58.830
Although it's a bit...

22:58.830 --> 23:01.130
Lame!

23:14.480 --> 23:18.190
The war goes on.

23:18.190 --> 23:20.620
Even if one side wins -

23:20.620 --> 23:23.220
- there will not be a place for us.

23:32.100 --> 23:35.200
If anything, this and now is...
